From: postmarketOS klte experiment <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd: free the message queue buffers in
 exit_dma

qcom_slim_ngd_init_dma() allocates the RX and TX message queue buffers
with dma_alloc_coherent() every time the NGD is set up, i.e. on every
runtime resume, but qcom_slim_ngd_exit_dma() only releases the DMA
channels and never frees the buffers.

With a 100 ms autosuspend delay any periodic SLIMbus register access
(e.g. a codec jack poll every 500 ms) cycles the controller through
suspend/resume continuously and leaks two coherent buffers per cycle.
On ARM32 each one is remapped into the 240 MiB vmalloc area, which is
exhausted after about 1.5 hours: kernel stack allocation in fork()
fails and userspace (the whole Phosh session) dies.

Free both buffers in qcom_slim_ngd_exit_dma() and clear the pointers,
also on the RX post error path so they are never freed twice.

---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -702,6 +702,7 @@

 rx_post_err:
 	dma_free_coherent(dev, size, ctrl->rx_base, ctrl->rx_phys_base);
+	ctrl->rx_base = NULL;
 rel_rx:
 	dma_release_channel(ctrl->dma_rx_channel);
 	return ret;
@@ -1131,6 +1132,8 @@

 static int qcom_slim_ngd_exit_dma(struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl *ctrl)
 {
+	struct device *dev = ctrl->dev;
+
 	if (ctrl->dma_rx_channel) {
 		dmaengine_terminate_sync(ctrl->dma_rx_channel);
 		dma_release_channel(ctrl->dma_rx_channel);
@@ -1143,6 +1146,18 @@

 	ctrl->dma_tx_channel = ctrl->dma_rx_channel = NULL;

+	if (ctrl->rx_base) {
+		dma_free_coherent(dev, QCOM_SLIM_NGD_DESC_NUM * SLIM_MSGQ_BUF_LEN,
+				  ctrl->rx_base, ctrl->rx_phys_base);
+		ctrl->rx_base = NULL;
+	}
+
+	if (ctrl->tx_base) {
+		dma_free_coherent(dev, (QCOM_SLIM_NGD_DESC_NUM + 1) * SLIM_MSGQ_BUF_LEN,
+				  ctrl->tx_base, ctrl->tx_phys_base);
+		ctrl->tx_base = NULL;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }

